From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:36:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [gbinder-radio] Hold the request while its response is
 handled

radio_base_handle_resp() takes the request out of the pending table
before completing it. If that drops what was left of its references,
radio_request_free() runs from there: it drops the request from the
active table and completes it as failed, though the response said it
succeeded. On a Qualcomm HIDL RIL this made every
iccTransmitApduLogicalChannel reply, and so oFono's UmtsAuthenticate,
fail (mer-hybris/libgbinder-radio#44).

Hold a reference for the length of the handler, as the issue proposes
and as upstream has taken into PR #39.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/mer-hybris/libgbinder-radio/pull/39]
---
 src/radio_base.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/radio_base.c b/src/radio_base.c
index 9af0252..56f11ca 100644
--- a/src/radio_base.c
+++ b/src/radio_base.c
@@ -834,7 +834,13 @@ radio_base_handle_resp(
     if (req) {
         RadioRequestRetryFunc retry = req->retry;
 
-        /* Temporary ref */
+        /*
+         * Temporary refs. Taking the request out of the pending table
+         * below may drop what would otherwise be its last reference, and
+         * freeing it from here completes it as failed, the response
+         * notwithstanding.
+         */
+        radio_request_ref(req);
         g_object_ref(self);
 
         /* It's no longer pending */
@@ -879,6 +885,7 @@ radio_base_handle_resp(
 
         radio_base_submit_queued_requests(self);
         radio_base_reset_timeout(self);
+        radio_request_unref(req);
         g_object_unref(self);
         return TRUE;
     }
